# Untitled

Fabrication of bimetallic metal–organic frameworks derived cobalt iron alloy@carbon–carbon nanotubes composites as ultrathin and high-efficiency microwave absorbers
Ruiwen Shu a,b,∗, Yue Wu b, Xiaohui Li b, Ningning Li b, Jianjun Shi b
a State Key Laboratory of Mining Response and Disaster Prevention and Control in Deep Coal Mines, Anhui University of Science and Technology, Huainan 232001, China b School of Chemical Engineering, Anhui University of Science and Technology, Huainan 232001, China
## h i g h l i g h t s
• Nitrogen-doped CoFe alloy@C–CNTs composites derived from MOFs were fabricated. • The attained composites presented a unique four-pointed star morphology. • Microwave absorption properties were modulated by regulating pyrolysis temperature. • The optimal minimum reflection loss reached \(-54.5\) dB at a thin thickness of \(1.4\;\mathrm{mm}\) . • Maximum effective absorption bandwidth achieved 5.6 GHz at a thickness of \(1.5~\mathrm{mm}\) .
